@startuml generations
!include _theme.puml

title Rebuilds and rollbacks — every change is reversible

state "Generation 1\nthe machine as installed" as g1
state "Generation 2\nafter you add a bundle" as g2
state "Generation 3\nafter a change that misbehaves" as g3

[*] --> g1 : install
g1 --> g2 : gisnix update
g2 --> g3 : gisnix update
g3 --> g2 : pick generation 2\nin the boot menu

note right of g3
  A rebuild never edits the running system.
  It builds a whole new generation and
  switches to it, keeping the old ones. If a
  change is wrong, reboot and choose the
  previous generation — you are exactly
  where you were.
end note
@enduml
